+### Refunds 
+
+Alipay requires that you submit a refund within 90 days from the original payment using the [Dashboard](https://dashboard.stripe.com/payments) or [Refunds API](https://docs.stripe.com/api/refunds/create.md). This is the maximum the payment method allows. Your return policy determines what you offer customers.
+
+Refunds for Alipay payments are asynchronous and take up to 5 minutes to complete. You can’t cancel Alipay refunds.
+
+#### Refund process 
+
+Alipay refunds are never processed as reversals. Alipay handles the refund directly and returns the funds to the customer’s original payment source, which is either their Alipay balance or linked payment method. The customer sees the refund reflected in their Alipay account or funding source.
+
+#### Tracking refunds 
+
+To check a refund’s status, open the payment in the [Dashboard](https://dashboard.stripe.com/payments) and click **View details** on the refund entry. You can also [retrieve the Refund object](https://docs.stripe.com/api/refunds/retrieve.md) and check its `status` field.
+
+Stripe notifies you of the final status through a `refund.updated` or `refund.failed` *webhook* (A webhook is a real-time push notification sent to your application as a JSON payload through HTTPS requests) event. [Verify webhook signatures](https://docs.stripe.com/webhooks.md#verify-events) to confirm that events came from Stripe. You can also use Stripe’s [public IP addresses](https://docs.stripe.com/ips.md) for network allowlisting. When a refund succeeds, the [Refund object](https://docs.stripe.com/api/refunds/object.md) status changes to `succeeded`. If the refund fails, the status changes to `failed` and Stripe returns the amount to your Stripe balance. You must refund the customer using another method.
+
+### Disputes 
+
+Alipay requires customers to authenticate payments directly with the Alipay app, which reduces the risk of fraud and unrecognized transactions. As a result, Alipay doesn’t support the standard dispute process—customers can’t file a chargeback, and funds are never withdrawn from your Stripe balance because of a dispute.
+
+If a customer contacts Alipay about a payment, they might be directed back to you. You can then issue a full or partial refund.
