+## Customer experience 
+
+#### 1. Select Alipay
+
+The customer selects Alipay at checkout.
+
+#### 2. Open Alipay
+
+On mobile, the customer continues in the Alipay app or mobile website. On desktop, the customer signs in to Alipay or scans the displayed QR code with the Alipay app.
+
+#### 3. Authorize the payment
+
+The customer reviews the amount and exchange rate, then authorizes the payment in Alipay within 5 minutes.
+
+#### 4. Return to the merchant
+
+After the payment succeeds, the customer returns to the merchant page and sees the completed payment.
+
+### Statement descriptors 
+
+Stripe sends Alipay a merchant name and an order description as separate fields. When you provide a statement descriptor for the payment, Stripe uses it as the order description. Otherwise, Stripe uses your account-level statement descriptor.
+
+Alipay controls how these fields appear in the customer’s Alipay transaction history and might localize, shorten, reformat, or omit them. Stripe doesn’t combine the fields into a fixed descriptor such as `ALIPAY*MERCHANT`.
+
+Stripe can’t guarantee the descriptor shown by a linked bank or card issuer. That funding transaction occurs between the customer, Alipay, and the issuer, and might display Alipay, an Alipay processing entity, merchant information supplied by Alipay, or an issuer-specific value. Don’t promise that your Stripe legal name or statement descriptor will appear verbatim on the customer’s funding-source statement.
+
+For Connect integrations, see [statement descriptors with Connect](https://docs.stripe.com/connect/statement-descriptors.md).
+
+To reconcile an Alipay payment with Alipay’s records, expand or retrieve the PaymentIntent’s `latest_charge`, then read:
+
+```text
+payment_intent.latest_charge.payment_method_details.alipay.transaction_id
+```
+
+## Enable Alipay 
+
+If you use Stripe front-end products, enable Alipay in your [payment method settings](https://dashboard.stripe.com/settings/payment_methods). Stripe automatically determines which payment methods are most relevant to each customer.
+
+If your integration lists payment methods manually, learn how to [configure Alipay as a payment method](https://docs.stripe.com/payments/alipay/accept-a-payment.md).
+
+Alipay supports destination charges and separate charges and transfers. Connected accounts with standard Dashboard access can enable Alipay in the Dashboard.
+
+For connected accounts without standard Dashboard access, the platform must request the `alipay_payments` capability. Requesting this capability through the API is in private preview. Before creating direct charges or using `on_behalf_of`, [contact Stripe Support](https://support.stripe.com/contact/email?topic=payment_apis) to request access.